        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;border-radius:6cqw;background:#f0fdfa;border:.9cqw solid #0f766e;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden'><svg viewBox='0 0 64 64' style='width:50cqw;height:50cqw;display:block' aria-hidden='true'><circle cx='32' cy='32' r='31' fill='#0f766e' opacity='.14'/><circle cx='32' cy='25' r='11' fill='#0f766e'/><path d='M11 56Q13 38 32 38Q51 38 53 56Z' fill='#0f766e'/></svg></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Icon: just the face, for when the profile is seen smaller than a card. The Method writes it.",
        "link": "",
        "reason": "A profile is recognised by its person: at the size where a card has no room for a name, the face is what says whose profile it is, and a glyph alone is only a mark."
